From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: flush before a declared feedback-loop draw on a7xx, for ARMSX2

From ARMSX2's Turnip (bmdhacks/armsx2-turnip, axfl2, "tu: flush before
a declared feedback-loop draw on a7xx"). A draw whose state declares an
attachment feedback loop gets the flush a colour-write to fragment-read
barrier would have produced: CCU colour clean, cache invalidate, wait
for idle. ARMSX2's GS drops its own barrier before such a draw on a
Turnip that does this.

Here it is on only for the engine named ARMSX2, which ARMSX2 gives
RetroArch through libretro's Vulkan context negotiation, so every other
application keeps stock behaviour and its own barriers. ARMSX2's driver
check, which looks for its packs' "git-axfl2-" tag, is patched to trust
this build instead (armsx2-lr 005).

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.h
@@ -491,6 +491,12 @@
    bool use_z24uint_s8uint;
    bool use_lrz;
 
+   /* A draw that declares an attachment feedback loop is flushed against the
+    * draws before it, so the application can leave out its own barrier. For
+    * ARMSX2 only, which drops its barriers for it.
+    */
+   bool feedback_loop_flush;
+
    struct fd_rd_output rd_output;
 
    /* This is an internal queue for mapping/unmapping non-sparse BOs */
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -3238,6 +3238,15 @@
        !physical_device->instance->drirc.misc.enable_d24s8_border_color_workaround);
    device->use_lrz = !TU_DEBUG_START(NOLRZ);
 
+   /* ARMSX2 names itself as the engine through libretro's Vulkan context
+    * negotiation, and RetroArch creates the instance with it.
+    */
+   device->feedback_loop_flush =
+      physical_device->instance->vk.app_info.engine_name &&
+      !strcmp(physical_device->instance->vk.app_info.engine_name, "ARMSX2");
+   if (device->feedback_loop_flush)
+      mesa_logi("tu: flushing before declared feedback-loop draws, for ARMSX2");
+
    tu_gpu_tracepoint_config_variable();
 
    device->submit_count = 0;
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -8665,6 +8665,24 @@
    if (cmd->state.dirty & TU_CMD_DIRTY_FS)
       tu_flush_dynamic_input_attachments<CHIP>(cmd);
 
+   /* From ARMSX2's Turnip (axfl2, "tu: flush before a declared feedback-loop
+    * draw on a7xx"), for ARMSX2 only. A draw whose state declares an
+    * attachment feedback loop, by the pipeline create flag or
+    * vkCmdSetAttachmentFeedbackLoopEnableEXT, gets the flush a colour-write to
+    * fragment-read barrier would have produced, so the application can drop
+    * that barrier. On an Adreno 740 the CCU clean and the wait for idle are
+    * both needed; without either, pictures differ from run to run. This
+    * orders the draw against earlier draws only: overlapping primitives
+    * within it are ordered by the sysmem prim mode a feedback loop already
+    * selects. A declared loop disables gmem, so these draws run in sysmem.
+    */
+   if (CHIP == A7XX && cmd->device->feedback_loop_flush &&
+       (cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state.feedback_loops |
+        cmd->state.pipeline_feedback_loops) != 0)
+      cmd->state.renderpass_cache.flush_bits |=
+         TU_CMD_FLAG_CCU_CLEAN_COLOR | TU_CMD_FLAG_CACHE_INVALIDATE |
+         TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_FOR_IDLE;
+
    tu_emit_cache_flush_renderpass<CHIP>(cmd);
 
   if (BITSET_TEST(cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state.dirty,
